 "site": {
  "reason": "an old post town on the pass road: lodgings, stores and the lord's watch on the north pass; slate from its quarry, wool from the summer pastures and timber from the valley's larches go down to Cogsworth. Its trade over the pass stopped when the Starfall brought the rockfall down, and the lord sealed the pass: the road beyond waits for a later region",
  "terrain": "a sheltered valley on the upper Cog inside the range: Garth Street along the valley floor, the temple on its plinth up the east slope, terraces stepping down to the river, snow on the peaks round it",
  "fit": "an old post town on the pass road: Garth Street along the valley floor, the temple on its stone plinth up the slope, the farmhouses on the upper terraces, the paddies stepping down on stone walls; the watch keep faces the sealed pass",
  "dry": false,
  "fortified": false,
